[[:db/cas 17592186101952 :tutorial/content "Suppose we are given the following matrix:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe denote the entry that lies at the intersection of the $\\color{blue}3$rd row and $\\color{red}2$nd column using the notation $a_{{\\color{blue}3}\\color{red}2}.$\n\nThe first subscript represents the row and the second subscript represents the column. So $a_{{\\color{blue}3}\\color{red}2}=8,$ as shown below.\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & \\boxed{8} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe can denote every entry of a matrix in this way.\nFor instance, $a_{{\\color{blue}4}\\color{red}1}$ denotes the entry that lies at the intersection of the $\\color{blue}4$th row and $\\color{red}1$st column.\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & {a}_{13} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & {a}_{23} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32} & {a}_{33} \\\\ {a}_{41} & {a}_{42} & {a}_{43}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "Suppose we are given the following matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe denote the entry that lies at the intersection of the $\\color{blue}3$rd row and $\\color{red}2$nd column using the notation $a_{{\\color{blue}3}\\color{red}2}.$\n\nThe first subscript represents the row and the second subscript represents the column. So $a_{{\\color{blue}3}\\color{red}2}=8,$ as shown below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & \\boxed{8} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can denote every entry of a matrix in this way.\nFor instance, $a_{{\\color{blue}4}\\color{red}1}$ denotes the entry that lies at the intersection of the $\\color{blue}4$th row and $\\color{red}1$st column.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & {a}_{13} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & {a}_{23} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32} & {a}_{33} \\\\ {a}_{41} & {a}_{42} & {a}_{43}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186100683 :question/problem "Find the entry $a_{23}$ of the matrix ${A},$ where \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "Find the entry $a_{23}$ of the matrix ${A},$ where \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186100683 :question/worked-solution "The entry $a_{23}$ lies at the intersection of the $2$nd row and $3$rd column. Therefore, $a_{23}={\\color{blue}{-3}}.$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "The entry $a_{23}$ lies at the intersection of the $2$nd row and $3$rd column. Therefore, $a_{23}={\\color{blue}{-3}}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186295053 :question/problem "Find the entry ${y}_{22}$ of the matrix $Y$, where \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Find the entry ${y}_{22}$ of the matrix $Y$, where \n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186295053 :question/worked-solution "The entry ${y}_{22}$ lies at the intersection of the $2$nd row and $2$nd column. Therefore, ${y}_{22}=-1.$\n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "The entry ${y}_{22}$ lies at the intersection of the $2$nd row and $2$nd column. Therefore, ${y}_{22}=-1.$\n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 6 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186295088 :question/problem "Find the entry ${e}_{53}$ of the matrix $E$, where \n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -2 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 3 & -8 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 5 & -8 \\\\ 6 & 6 & -6 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 4 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n${e}_{53}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Find the entry ${e}_{53}$ of the matrix $E$, where \n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -2 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 3 & -8 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 5 & -8 \\\\ 6 & 6 & -6 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 4 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n${e}_{53}=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186295088 :question/worked-solution "The entry ${e}_{53}$ lies at the intersection of the $5$th row and $3$rd column. Therefore, ${e}_{53}=2.$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -2 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 3 & -8 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 5 & -8 \\\\ 6 & 6 & -6 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 4 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "The entry ${e}_{53}$ lies at the intersection of the $5$th row and $3$rd column. Therefore, ${e}_{53}=2.$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -2 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 3 & -8 & -2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 5 & -8 \\\\ 6 & 6 & -6 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 4 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186295089 :question/problem "Find the entry ${f}_{32}$ of the matrix $F$, where \n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n${f}_{32}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Find the entry ${f}_{32}$ of the matrix $F$, where \n\n$$\nF=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n${f}_{32}=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186295089 :question/worked-solution "The entry ${f}_{32}$ lies at the intersection of the $3$rd row and $2$nd column. Therefore, ${f}_{32}=4.$\n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "The entry ${f}_{32}$ lies at the intersection of the $3$rd row and $2$nd column. Therefore, ${f}_{32}=4.$\n\n$$\nF=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186395748 :question/problem "Find the entry ${c}_{24}$ of the matrix $C$, where \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Find the entry ${c}_{24}$ of the matrix $C$, where \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186395748 :question/worked-solution "The entry ${c}_{24}$ should lie at the intersection of the $2$nd row and $4$th column. Therefore, ${c}_{24}=5.$\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "The entry ${c}_{24}$ should lie at the intersection of the $2$nd row and $4$th column. Therefore, ${c}_{24}=5.$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186398263 :question/problem "Find the entry ${e}_{31}$ of the matrix $E$, where \n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Find the entry ${e}_{31}$ of the matrix $E$, where \n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186398263 :question/worked-solution "The entry ${e}_{31}$ lies at the intersection of the $3$rd row and $1$st column. Therefore, ${e}_{31}=-3.$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "The entry ${e}_{31}$ lies at the intersection of the $3$rd row and $1$st column. Therefore, ${e}_{31}=-3.$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186100684 :question/problem "Find the entry $b_{22}$ of the matrix ${B},$ where \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "Find the entry $b_{22}$ of the matrix ${B},$ where \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186100684 :question/worked-solution "The entry $b_{22}$ lies at the intersection of the $2$nd row and $2$nd column. Therefore, $b_{22}={\\color{blue}{2}}.$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "The entry $b_{22}$ lies at the intersection of the $2$nd row and $2$nd column. Therefore, $b_{22}={\\color{blue}{2}}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186101124 :question/problem "Find the entry ${a}_{32}$ of the matrix $A$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Find the entry ${a}_{32}$ of the matrix $A$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186101124 :question/worked-solution "The entry ${a}_{32}$ lies at the intersection of the $3$rd row and $2$nd column. Therefore, ${a}_{32}=8.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "The entry ${a}_{32}$ lies at the intersection of the $3$rd row and $2$nd column. Therefore, ${a}_{32}=8.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186269010 :question/problem "Find the entry ${g}_{22}$ of the matrix $G$, where \n\n$$\nG=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Find the entry ${g}_{22}$ of the matrix $G$, where \n\n$$\nG=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186269010 :question/worked-solution "The entry ${g}_{22}$ lies at the intersection of the $2$nd row and $2$nd column. Therefore, ${g}_{22}=2.$\n\n$$\nG=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "The entry ${g}_{22}$ lies at the intersection of the $2$nd row and $2$nd column. Therefore, ${g}_{22}=2.$\n\n$$\nG=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186295090 :question/problem "Find the entry ${a}_{22}$ of the matrix $A$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\n${a}_{22}=$\n{{field-1}}" "Find the entry ${a}_{22}$ of the matrix $A$, where \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\n${a}_{22}=$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186295090 :question/worked-solution "The entry ${a}_{22}$ lies at the intersection of the $2$nd row and $2$nd column. Therefore, ${a}_{22}=-3.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "The entry ${a}_{22}$ lies at the intersection of the $2$nd row and $2$nd column. Therefore, ${a}_{22}=-3.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186398270 :question/problem "Find the entry ${r}_{43}$ of the matrix $R$, where \n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Find the entry ${r}_{43}$ of the matrix $R$, where \n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186398270 :question/worked-solution "The entry ${r}_{43}$ lies at the intersection of the $4$th row and $3$rd column. Therefore, ${r}_{43}=1.$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "The entry ${r}_{43}$ lies at the intersection of the $4$th row and $3$rd column. Therefore, ${r}_{43}=1.$\n\n$$\nR=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186400191 :question/problem "Find the entry ${b}_{32}$ of the matrix $B$, where \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "Find the entry ${b}_{32}$ of the matrix $B$, where \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186101953 :tutorial/content "In general, we denote the entry of a matrix $A$ that lies at the intersection of the $\\color{blue}i$th row and $\\color{red}j$th column by $a_{{\\color{blue}i}\\color{red}j}.$\n\nIf $A$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix, we can write it as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & … & {a}_{1n} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & … & {a}_{2n} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ {a}_{m1} & {a}_{m2} & … & {a}_{mn}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhere each entry $a_{ij}$ is defined for $i = 1,2,\\ldots,m$ and $j =1,2,\\ldots,n.$" "In general, we denote the entry of a matrix $A$ that lies at the intersection of the $\\color{blue}i$th row and $\\color{red}j$th column by $a_{{\\color{blue}i}\\color{red}j}.$\n\nIf $A$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix, we can write it as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & \\cdots & {a}_{1n} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & \\cdots & {a}_{2n} \\\\ \\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\ {a}_{m1} & {a}_{m2} & \\cdots & {a}_{mn}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhere each entry $a_{ij}$ is defined for $i = 1,2,\\ldots,m$ and $j =1,2,\\ldots,n.$"] [:db/cas 17592186100685 :question/problem "Consider the highlighted entry of the matrix $C$ given below. Describe it in terms of $c_{ij}.$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 34 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "Consider the highlighted entry of the matrix $C$ given below. Describe it in terms of $c_{ij}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & \\boxed{5} \\\\ 34 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186101126 :question/problem "Consider the highlighted entry of the matrix $A$ given below. Describe it in terms of $a_{ij}$.\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 20 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 17 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$" "Consider the highlighted entry of the matrix $A$ given below. Describe it in terms of $a_{ij}$.\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & \\boxed{7} & 10 \\\\ 4 & 20 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 17 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186101127 :question/problem "Consider the highlighted entry of the matrix $B$ given below. Describe it in terms of $b_{ij}$.\n\n$B = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 10 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 14 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 17 & 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" "Consider the highlighted entry of the matrix $B$ given below. Describe it in terms of $b_{ij}$.\n\n$B = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 10 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 14 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 17 & \\boxed{9} & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186235399 :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIn index notation, the highlighted entry of the matrix $P$ above is ${p}_{ij},$ where$\\,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $i=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         and \n$j=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & \\boxed{2} & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn index notation, the highlighted entry of the matrix $P$ above is ${p}_{ij},$ where$\\,$\n\n$i=$\n\n{{field-1}}\n\nand\n$j=$\n\n{{field-2}}\n\n."] [:db/cas 17592186269009 :question/problem "Consider the highlighted entry of the matrix $C$ given below. Describe it in terms of ${c}_{ij}.$\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "Consider the highlighted entry of the matrix $C$ given below. Describe it in terms of ${c}_{ij}.$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix} \\boxed{1} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186295091 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $B$ given by\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn terms of ${b}_{ij},$ the highlighted entry of the matrix $B$ corresponds to{{field-1}}." "Consider the matrix $B$ given by\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix} \\boxed{-2} & -3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn terms of ${b}_{ij},$ the highlighted entry of the matrix $B$ corresponds to{{field-1}}."] [:db/cas 17592186295092 :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn terms of ${a}_{ij},$ the highlighted entry of the matrix $A$ corresponds to{{field-1}}." "Consider the matrix $A$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\boxed{5} \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn terms of ${a}_{ij},$ the highlighted entry of the matrix $A$ corresponds to{{field-1}}."] [:db/cas 17592186400198 :question/problem "Consider the highlighted entry of the matrix $Y$ given below. Describe it in terms of ${y}_{ij}.$\n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "Consider the highlighted entry of the matrix $Y$ given below. Describe it in terms of ${y}_{ij}.$\n\n$$\nY=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\boxed{7} \\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186400702 :question/problem "Consider the highlighted entry of the matrix $A$ given below. Describe it in terms of ${a}_{ij}.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 10 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 14 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 17 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "Consider the highlighted entry of the matrix $A$ given below. Describe it in terms of ${a}_{ij}.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 10 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 14 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 9 & 17 & 9 & \\boxed{0} \\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186493306 :question/problem "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{0} & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIn index notation, the highlighted entry of the matrix $P$ above is ${p}_{ij},$ where$\\,$\n\n$i=$\n\n{{field-1}}\n\nand\n$j=$\n\n{{field-2}}\n\n." "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{0} & -2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn index notation, the highlighted entry of the matrix $P$ above is ${p}_{ij},$ where$\\,$\n\n$i=$\n\n{{field-1}}\n\nand\n$j=$\n\n{{field-2}}\n\n."]]
